.TH SYSMON 1 "November 2026" "sysmon 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysmon \- graphical system monitor for Raspberry Pi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysmon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysmon
shows live rolling charts of CPU utilization, disk I/O, network I/O,
CPU and drive temperatures, and fan speed, updating every second with
60 seconds of history. It requires a graphical desktop session.
.PP
Drive temperatures are read with
.BR "sudo smartctl" ,
so the user must be able to run
.B smartctl
through
.B sudo
without a password.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sysmon.ini
Configuration file for hiding drives and network interfaces,
setting a case fan tachometer GPIO pin, and passing extra
.B smartctl
options. If it does not exist when the package is installed, it is
generated from the hardware: the loopback interface
.B lo
is hidden; if the root filesystem is on an NVMe drive,
.B mmcblk0
is hidden; and on an Argon ONE UP,
.B eth0
(which is not wired to a port) is hidden. An existing file is never
changed, and it is removed when the package is purged. If the file is
missing when sysmon starts, the same rules are applied in memory. An
annotated example is installed at
.IR /usr/share/doc/sysmon/examples/sysmon.ini .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysmon/venv
Python virtual environment the application runs in, created when the
package is configured.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartctl (8)
